  {
    "title": "Which two claims are correct?",
    "tag": "AP-STYLE · SELECT TWO",
    "time": "80–83 min",
    "code": "AAP-2.P · AAP-4.A.6",
    "html": "<ol><li>A. Binary search requires sorted data for its elimination rule.</li><li>B. Binary search always checks the first element first.</li><li>C. Correct algorithms can have the same result and different costs.</li><li>D. A missing target makes binary search continue forever.</li></ol><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class=\"answer\"><strong>A and C.</strong> Binary starts at a midpoint and stops when candidates are exhausted.</div></details>",
    "note": "两项全对才得一分。B混淆linear，D忽略空候选停止；让学生口述未找到28的最后一步。使用原创练习，并区分“完整列表为空”与“剩余区间为空”。"
  },
  {
    "title": "Homework and the next lesson",
